hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"76","On prostration. Muhammad ibn Adam narrated to us, Abu Khalid narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Zayd ibn Aslam, who said: A boy recited the verse of prostration before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); the boy waited for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to prostrate, and when he did not prostrate, he said: O Messenger of Allah, is there not a prostration in it? He said: You are the one who recited it; had you prostrated, we would have prostrated."
"77","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Mahri narrated to us, Ibn Wahb informed us; Hisham ibn Sa'd and Hafs ibn Maysarah informed me, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, who said: It reached me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)... and he mentioned the like of it."
"78","Ahmad ibn Amr ibn al-Sarh narrated to us, Ibn Wahb informed us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Salih, from Amir ibn Jushayb, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Surah al-Hajj has been favored over the rest of the Qur'an with two prostrations. Abu Dawud said: This has also been given a connected chain, but it is not authentic."
